# FLOW_JOURNAL Incident 86: prove that Yosys' `fsm` pass (the FSM re-encoding that OpenLane's
# synthesis applies) preserves the behaviour of the final RTL (rtl_r12b = 8b163675).
#
# EQY then compares the final netlist with gold = RTL + this same `fsm` pass. Together:
#   RTL  ==(this proof)==  RTL + fsm  ==(EQY)==  final netlist.
#
# Method: Yosys' own tool for exactly this. `fsm -encfile` writes the old -> new state codes;
# `equiv_make -encfile` builds the equivalence module with the gate state decoded through
# that table; equiv_simple / equiv_induct prove every $equiv cell; equiv_status -assert
# fails the script if any cell stays unproven.
#
# NEGATIVE CONTROL: equiv_make reads enc_neg.txt (en_phase codes 10 and 01 swapped); must FAIL

# RTL front end = the [script]+[gold] sections of the EQY script, as EQY writes gold.ys
script front_end.ys
proc
# the steps OpenLane's synthesis runs before `fsm` (openlane_synth: opt_expr, opt_clean,
# openlane_opt(nodffe, nosdff))
opt_expr
opt_clean
opt -nodffe -nosdff
design -save pre

fsm -encfile enc_neg_written.txt
design -save post

# identical back end on both copies: memories to flops, async resets to sync (SAT models)
design -load pre
memory -nomap
memory_map
async2sync
opt_clean
design -save pre_m
design -load post
memory -nomap
memory_map
async2sync
opt_clean
design -save post_m

design -reset
design -copy-from pre_m -as gold soc_asic_top
design -copy-from post_m -as gate soc_asic_top
design -copy-from pre_m sky130_sram_*
equiv_make -encfile enc_neg.txt gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
equiv_simple -seq 2
equiv_status
equiv_induct -seq 2
equiv_status -assert
